examples.solution_text:
Count each value to find its frequency. Include 4 even though nobody borrowed 4 books.

$\begin{array}{c|rrrrrr}\text{Books}&0&1&2&3&4&5\\\hline\text{Frequency}&2&3&3&1&0&1\end{array}$

Draw equally spaced ticks for every value from 0 to 5. Stack one equally sized dot for each student.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-0.5,0)--(5.5,0);
\foreach \x in {0,...,5} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.15) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\n in {0/2,1/3,2/3,3/1,5/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\n} {\fill[black] (\x,\k) circle (1.8pt);}}
\node at (2.5,4) {Books borrowed};
\node[below] at (2.5,-0.9) {Number of books};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b) There are 3 dots above 1, so 3 students borrowed exactly 1 book.

(c) More than 2 books means 3, 4 or 5 books.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}1+0+1\\&=2\text{ students}\end{aligned}$

(d) At least 3 books includes the same 2 students. Count all dots to find the total:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}2+3+3+1+0+1\\&=10\text{ students}\end{aligned}$

$\begin{aligned}\text{Percentage}&=\frac{2}{10}\times100\%\\&=20\%\end{aligned}$

examples.question_text:
The column graph shows sandwiches sold at a café.
(a) How many salad sandwiches were sold?
(b) How many more chicken than cheese sandwiches were sold?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=3mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8,10} {\draw[draw=gray!40] (0,\y)--(6,\y);}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,11);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(6.2,0);
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8,10} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[black] (0.6,0) rectangle (1.4,4);
\draw[black] (2.6,0) rectangle (3.4,7);
\draw[black] (4.6,0) rectangle (5.4,9);
\node[below] at (1,0) {Cheese};
\node[below] at (3,0) {Salad};
\node[below] at (5,0) {Chicken};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1,5) {Number sold};
\node[below] at (3,-2) {Sandwich type};
\node at (3,12.5) {Sandwiches sold};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The frequency histogram shows scores in a quiz.
(a) What is the frequency of score 4?
(b) Which scores are most frequent?

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=4mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \y in {2,4,6,8} {\draw[draw=gray!40] (0,\y)--(5,\y);}
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,8.8);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(5.2,0);
\foreach \y in {0,2,4,6,8} {\draw[black] (-0.1,\y)--(0,\y);\node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\draw[black] (0.5,0) rectangle (1.5,3);
\draw[black] (1.5,0) rectangle (2.5,7);
\draw[black] (2.5,0) rectangle (3.5,5);
\draw[black] (3.5,0) rectangle (4.5,7);
\foreach \x/\s in {1/2,2/3,3/4,4/5} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15);\node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (\x,-0.15) {$\s$};}
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.9,4) {Frequency};
\node[below] at (2.5,-1.5) {Score};
\node at (2.5,10) {Quiz scores};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
